[Music]  Thank You William and thank you all very  much for allowing me to address you  today your annual meeting which I hear  was changed specifically to accommodate  me so I do apologize for your Diaries  I'm especially pleased to do so as  supporting charities is the heart of  what I and the whole royal family do  that said as most of you will appreciate  no one not even me says no to William  Shawcross so I have no choice anyway so  I thought I start with something  personal a tribute to my parents I have  two children as you probably know I  gather it has been widely reported and  when I first became a father four and a  half years ago I began to process of  thinking about the way I'd been brought  up and the values that my parents are  they're still than me as any parent will  know this process is not necessarily one  that you want to take consciously you  find the certain values ones that you  didn't know you had to start bubbling up  to the surface some Wireless memories  relates times my parents spoke to me or  even better  showed me what it meant to have both  privilege and responsibilities  I remember being taken by my mother to a  homelessness shelter at a young age her  explaining to me why the people I met  there matter and why no society can be  healthy unless we take other people  seriously for my father I learned how  central charity was or how central China  was to his life and his sense of purpose  the Prince's Trust is not an  arm's-length organization for my father  he cares deeply about the princess trust  because it is a living projection of his  values as a young child I recall evening  after evening my father's diligence and  compassion as he applied himself to  answering thousands of letters and  reading endless reports in order to stay  on top of his ambition to do all he  could to help the underprivileged  without my realizing it's what my  parents were doing was distilling in me  and Harry a lifelong habits to put  charity at the heart of our lives my  father of course had inherited this very  same habit from his parents  my grandfather Prince Phillip has been  one of the most tireless public servants  of this country deeply committed to  helping young people fulfill their  potential my grandmother the Queen has  never given a Christmas broadcast  without paying tribute to charitable  organisations volunteers and people who  care for others my family have not done  this because it looks good they do  because charity is not an optional extra  in society we believe that above  anything else charities nurture repair  build and sustain our society  [Music]  you

